# Binary assets - not architecture, and every image here costs a vision
# subagent on every rebuild whose extraction cache has been invalidated.
#
# src/main/icons/  the app icon in ten sizes
# media/           recorded demos: GIFs, MP4s and stills
# examples/        the demo fixtures (dummy_1..10.jpg and a few text files)
# .../base/Icons/ the vendored Material icon set: 829 third-party SVGs, plus a
#                  manifest.json whose 8000 extension keys the AST extractor
#                  reads as 496 symbols - one giant community of file
#                  extensions. It is data, not architecture. What fman does
#                  *with* it is impl/model/icon_set.py, which is not ignored.
# .../Core/Fonts/  the vendored Google Fonts: .ttf binaries and their
#                  licences. Same reason - the code that picks one is
#                  impl/themes.py and impl/plugins/plugin.py.
src/main/icons/
media/
examples/
src/main/resources/base/Icons/
src/main/resources/base/Plugins/Core/Fonts/
.venv/
